### Rooms module — manual requests (REST Client extension for VS Code)
#
# How to use:
# 1. Install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) in VS Code.
# 2. Open this file. Above each request block you'll see a small
#    "Send Request" link — click it to fire that specific request.
# 3. Make sure the API is running (npm run dev) before sending requests.
# 4. Edit the values in the JSON bodies freely to try different cases.
# 5. baseUrl comes from the active REST Client environment (bottom-right
#    of VS Code) — see .vscode/settings.json for "local" vs "production".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin token setup (needed for POST /rooms below)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no endpoint to register as ADMIN directly. Instead, run the seed
# script to create/update an admin user from the ADMIN_SEED_* vars in .env:
#   npm run prisma:seed
# Then log in with those credentials via auth/auth.http (POST /auth/login,
# using ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL/ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD from .env) and paste the
# returned accessToken below.
@adminToken = replace-with-admin-token

# Optional: a token from a regular (non-admin) user, used below to check
# the 403 case. Get it the normal way via POST /auth/login.
@userToken = replace-with-user-token

### List all rooms (requires auth — any logged-in user, no specific role)
# Requires @adminToken (or @userToken) to be set above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Create a room (happy path — admin only)
# Requires @adminToken to be set above (see setup instructions).
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Meeting Room A",
  "capacity": 6,
  "pricePerHour": 15.5
}

### Availability for a room (requires auth — any logged-in user, no specific role)
# Replace @roomId with the id of a room that already exists (e.g. copy it
# from the response of "List all rooms" above, or from the room you just
# created). Requires @adminToken (or @userToken) to be set above.
@roomId = replace-with-room-id
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/availability?date=2026-09-15
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Error case: create a room without the Authorization header
# No token at all — expect 401 Unauthorized.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unauthorized Room",
  "capacity": 4,
  "pricePerHour": 10
}

### Error case: create a room with a non-admin user's token
# Valid token, but the user's role isn't ADMIN — expect 403 Forbidden.
# Requires @userToken to be set above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "name": "Forbidden Room",
  "capacity": 4,
  "pricePerHour": 10
}

### Error case: create a room with negative capacity
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — capacity must be a positive integer.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Negative Capacity Room",
  "capacity": -3,
  "pricePerHour": 10
}

### Error case: create a room with a negative pricePerHour
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — pricePerHour must be a positive number.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Negative Price Room",
  "capacity": 4,
  "pricePerHour": -15.5
}

### Error case: create a room without a name
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — name is required.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "capacity": 4,
  "pricePerHour": 10
}

### Error case: availability with an invalid date format
# Expect 422 Unprocessable Entity — date must be YYYY-MM-DD.
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/availability?date=15-09-2026
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Error case: list rooms without the Authorization header
# No token at all — expect 401 Unauthorized.
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms

### Error case: availability without the Authorization header
# No token at all — expect 401 Unauthorized.
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/availability?date=2026-09-15
